From: fatalcoder524 <11532648+fatalcoder524@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: gadget: udc: add a gadget state notifier

usb_gadget_set_state() is the single point where the UDC state changes, but it
only does schedule_work(&gadget->work), whose worker just calls
sysfs_notify(&udc->dev.kobj, NULL, "state").  Userspace can poll(2) that node;
the kernel has no way to be told that the gadget reached "configured" or
"not attached".

Anything deciding behaviour from the gadget state - enabling adb only for a
real host rather than a charger, for example - therefore has to poll, or guess
from power supply events.  Power supply events do not report enumeration, so
such a driver silently never fires on boards whose charger driver stays quiet.

Add an atomic notifier chain fired from usb_gadget_set_state(), named after the
existing usb_gadget_register_driver().  Callbacks receive the state that was
just set.  usb_gadget_set_state() is reachable from interrupt and UDC
completion context, hence atomic: callbacks must only schedule work.

Signed-off-by: fatalcoder524 <11532648+fatalcoder524@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/usb/gadget/udc/core.c | 15 +++++++++++++++
 include/linux/usb/gadget.h    |  7 +++++++
 2 files changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/gadget/udc/core.c b/drivers/usb/gadget/udc/core.c
@@ -1015,11 +1015,31 @@
 		sysfs_notify(&udc->dev.kobj, NULL, "state");
 }
 
+/*
+ * Atomic notifier chain: usb_gadget_set_state() is reachable from interrupt
+ * and UDC completion context, so callbacks must not sleep.  They get the
+ * state that was just set as the event value.
+ */
+static ATOMIC_NOTIFIER_HEAD(usb_gadget_state_notifier);
+
+int usb_gadget_register_state_notifier(struct notifier_block *nb)
+{
+	return atomic_notifier_chain_register(&usb_gadget_state_notifier, nb);
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(usb_gadget_register_state_notifier);
+
+void usb_gadget_unregister_state_notifier(struct notifier_block *nb)
+{
+	atomic_notifier_chain_unregister(&usb_gadget_state_notifier, nb);
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(usb_gadget_unregister_state_notifier);
+
 void usb_gadget_set_state(struct usb_gadget *gadget,
 		enum usb_device_state state)
 {
 	gadget->state = state;
 	schedule_work(&gadget->work);
+	atomic_notifier_call_chain(&usb_gadget_state_notifier, state, gadget);
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(usb_gadget_set_state);
 
diff --git a/include/linux/usb/gadget.h b/include/linux/usb/gadget.h
@@ -867,6 +867,13 @@
 extern void usb_gadget_set_state(struct usb_gadget *gadget,
 		enum usb_device_state state);
 
+/*
+ * Fired from usb_gadget_set_state() with the new state as the event value.
+ * Atomic context: schedule work, do not sleep.
+ */
+extern int usb_gadget_register_state_notifier(struct notifier_block *nb);
+extern void usb_gadget_unregister_state_notifier(struct notifier_block *nb);
+
 /*-------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
 
 /* utility to tell udc core that the bus reset occurs */
